{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125530-idea-different-dynamic-for-gauntlet-strength","id":1125530,"title":"[Idea] Different Dynamic for Gauntlet Strength","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-06T04:07:29-07:00","id":1125530,"title":"[Idea] Different Dynamic for Gauntlet Strength","content":"So, the Shadow. Where spirits roam in a kill-or-be-killed world. The Gauntlet is the only barrier between it and the Material Realm. The Gauntlet's Strength is higher in places of civilization, where several humans congregate and live, drowning out the primal Shadow in its constant noise. In the wilderness, where few humans live, if any at all, allowing the spirits to be closer to the world and a much weaker Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> \u200bNice concept in and of itself, but I think it's a bit limiting. What if Gauntlet Strength wasn't so much determined by human activity, but rather by the dynamics of the region. Specifically, how well the region reflects the nature of the Shadow. Places that reflect the kill-or-be-killed nature would have a weaker Gauntlet, whereas places of peace and tranquility have a stronger Gauntlet. By making this the factor for Gauntlet Strength, one can easily have a weak Gauntlet within bustling cities. Slums or kangaroo courts would have a weak Gauntlet, whereas oases and mountain summits would have a strong Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust an idea. Like it? Hate it? Already been posited? Doesn't work? Lemme know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T04:23:00-07:00","id":1125534,"title":"","content":"So, you are basically saying treat Gauntlet strength as the inverse of Resonance to the Shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:26:54-07:00","id":1125588,"title":"","content":"Sounds pretty much like Pangaea Depth from Sundered World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:18:42-07:00","id":1125603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125530-idea-different-dynamic-for-gauntlet-strength#post1125530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Shadow. Where spirits roam in a kill-or-be-killed world. The Gauntlet is the only barrier between it and the Material Realm. The Gauntlet's Strength is higher in places of civilization, where several humans congregate and live, drowning out the primal Shadow in its constant noise. In the wilderness, where few humans live, if any at all, allowing the spirits to be closer to the world and a much weaker Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> \u200bNice concept in and of itself, but I think it's a bit limiting. What if Gauntlet Strength wasn't so much determined by human activity, but rather by the dynamics of the region. Specifically, how well the region reflects the nature of the Shadow. Places that reflect the kill-or-be-killed nature would have a weaker Gauntlet, whereas places of peace and tranquility have a stronger Gauntlet. By making this the factor for Gauntlet Strength, one can easily have a weak Gauntlet within bustling cities. Slums or kangaroo courts would have a weak Gauntlet, whereas oases and mountain summits would have a strong Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust an idea. Like it? Hate it? Already been posited? Doesn't work? Lemme know.</div> </div> </div> </div>How literally are you accounting for the kill-or-be-killed resonance? Because let's say book burning in an attempt to extinguish an idea or emotion would be a good example of that mechanic aimed at conceptual spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, there's plenty of savagery in the wilds already, what with animals literally preying on one another. Not so much of that in cities, at least not without the actual concept of sheer survival being in the line, most of the time.<br /> <br /> Would different spirits which care for different resonances be affected by different things that promote life-and-death confrontations? (Boy, prisons would suck...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:42:11-07:00","id":1125637,"title":"","content":"I think it would be harder to quantify for games. We already get people who struggle with the idea of Influence and Resonance and other story-based powers and effects. Aside from that, you already have two big reasons for 'thin' Gauntlets in the city. Loci and beshilu. A locus is a place with a thinner Gauntlet than the wilderness, plus with a city where more things happen there's more likelihood of one forming, even through a thick Gauntlet. Once you throw humanity into the mix you have whole ranges of spirits that you wouldn't get in the wilderness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T15:21:11-07:00","id":1125706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125530-idea-different-dynamic-for-gauntlet-strength?p=1125637#post1125637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be harder to quantify for games. We already get people who struggle with the idea of Influence and Resonance and other story-based powers and effects. Aside from that, you already have two big reasons for 'thin' Gauntlets in the city. Loci and beshilu. A locus is a place with a thinner Gauntlet than the wilderness, plus with a city where more things happen there's more likelihood of one forming, even through a thick Gauntlet. Once you throw humanity into the mix you have whole ranges of spirits that you wouldn't get in the wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, one of the primary consequences of a thinner Gauntlet is that the place's Shadow bears more resemblance to its material counterpart; in the normal scheme of things this means that the spiritual reflections of cities are more heavily abstracted from the forms people are familiar with, in contrast to the more prosaic &quot;things are bigger or smaller than normal&quot; and &quot;new features haven't shown up yet or old features that are gone still show up&quot; manifestations common to less populated zones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}